            For most healthy adults who train, 1.6 g/kg of body weight per day (about 0.73 g/lb) is the number to beat, with 2.2 g/kg as a sensible ceiling and the higher end reserved for cutting. Sedentary adults can stay closer to the RDA, adults over 65 should aim for at least 1.0 to 1.2 g/kg, and anyone with obesity should calculate from a realistic goal weight rather than current weight.
